    {
      "text": "witnesses to Book of Mormon, D&C 5: Intro. Joseph Smith to stand as witness of plates, D&C 5:2 (14:8). what greater witness can God give, D&C 6:23. every word to be established by two or three witnesses, D&C 6:28 (128:3). the Holy Ghost gives utterance, to stand as witness, D&C 14:8. world judged by witnesses, D&C 20:13. elders bear witness to the Majesty on high, D&C 20:16. partakers of sacrament witness they will take Christ’s name, keep commandments, remember him, D&C 20:77, 79. Apostles are especial witnesses of the Lord’s name, D&C 27:12 (107:23, 26). at trial of adulterer, two or more witnesses required, D&C 42:80–81. two witnesses are two prophets raised to Jewish nation, D&C 77:15. Seventies are especial witnesses, D&C 107:25. recorder to be eye-witness to baptisms, D&C 127:6 (128:2). the Lord has left a witness of his name, D&C 136:40.",
